\fs24 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 short description: 
\f1\fs26 Bone Bone uses discarded cow bones as moulds for glass vessels, turning a by-product of meat production into a tool for making.
\f0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\

\fs24 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 description: 
\f1\fs26 Bone Bone starts with a material that is usually left behind: cow bone from meat production. Used as a mould for molten glass, the hollow bones give the vessels their irregular, organic forms. The heat blackens and alters the bones as the glass takes shape inside them. What begins as a discarded material becomes part of the making process and gains another function. The resulting vessels carry both the physical imprint of the bone and the history of its transformation.
